From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 12:21:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Wire attach_shadow through the mutator + shadow-aware
 lifecycle

attach_shadow creates the shadow-root node, parents it to the host
while keeping it OUT of host.children (parent pointer preserves the
mark_ancestors_dirty chain across the boundary; absence from children
keeps light-tree walks blind), and mirrors the host's in-document
flag so later appends into the root propagate flags correctly via
add_children_to_parent's existing logic.

Lifecycle holes this also plugs: drop_node_ignoring_parent recurses
into attached shadow trees (else their slab slots leak and freed ids
get recycled under live references); deep_clone_node clears the
cloned host's shadow_root (raw copy would alias the original's tree
by node id - spec says clones never copy shadow roots); and
iter_subtree_mut recurses through shadow roots so insertion/removal
processing (IS_IN_DOCUMENT, id map, stylesheet/image special ops)
follows the host subtree it rides in.

Known M1 gap, fixed with query boundaries later: shadow-tree ids now
land in the document-level nodes_to_id map (getElementById can see -
or be clobbered by - shadow content).
